{
  "manufacturer": "Contemporary Controls",
  "manufacturer_slug": "contemporary-controls",
  "model": "Danfoss VLT HVAC Drive FC 102 via BASgatewayLX",
  "short_model": "BASgatewayLX Danfoss FC102",
  "model_slug": "basgatewaylx-danfoss-fc102",
  "aliases": [
    "FC102",
    "FC 102",
    "VLT HVAC Drive",
    "Danfoss FC-102 Modbus"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive (HVAC)",
  "applies_to": "Danfoss VLT HVAC Drive FC 102 on Modbus RTU (FC protocol set to Modbus), read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for the Danfoss FC 102: 97 objects (65 AI, 32 BI), 94 polled by default. It reads the control and status words (with each status bit split out as a Binary Input), references, power, voltage, current, frequency, temperatures, I/O states and the alarm, warning and extended status words. All objects are inputs, so it is a monitoring profile.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Danfoss_FC102_Drive_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the Danfoss FC 102 Modbus register spreadsheet (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/DanfossFC102.xls).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "Only 94 of the 97 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
    "Some names appear more than once in the profile as published (Not Used); they are kept as printed and told apart by instance."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Danfoss_FC102_Drive",
    "doc_number": "Danfoss_FC102_Drive_LX.csv",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/Danfoss_FC102_Drive_LX.zip"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Poll Running, Auto Mode, Alarm and Warning plus the actual values. Writing start/stop or a reference needs output objects that this profile does not include.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BI 89",
        "name": "Running",
        "why": "Drive running"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 87",
        "name": "Auto Mode",
        "why": "Drive in auto (remote) mode"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 10",
        "name": "Frequency",
        "why": "Output frequency"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 11",
        "name": "Motor Current",
        "why": "Motor current"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 7",
        "name": "Input Power [kW]",
        "why": "Input power, kW"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 5",
        "name": "Main Actual Value [%]",
        "why": "Main actual value, %"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 85",
        "name": "Warning",
        "why": "Any active warning"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 81",
        "name": "Alarm",
        "why": "Any active alarm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 55",
        "name": "Alarm Word",
        "why": "Alarm word (bit-coded)"
      }
    ],
    "enable": null,
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "The BASgatewayLX presents each Modbus device as its own virtual BACnet device on BACnet IP; give it a unique device instance and Modbus address (serial) or IP address (Modbus TCP) when you add it with this profile.",
      "One BASgatewayLX handles up to 100 Modbus devices and 1000 polled points in total, so leave unneeded rows unpolled."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "The profile is read-only: it has no output objects, so start/stop and speed reference cannot be written through it as published.",
      "The profile carries no units; the names give them (e.g. Input Power [kW], Torque [Nm]).",
      "Unpolled rows do not appear as BACnet objects until enabled in the gateway's device profile page."
    ]
  },
